However, having taken into consideration the amount involved in the present case and the fact that co-accused i.e. son of applicant, has also been granted permission to travel abroad at the same time, this Court deems it appropriate to impose the following conditions upon the applicant:
a) The petitioner shall furnish a Bank Guarantee of Rs. 1,00,00,000/- (Rupees One Crore), to the concerned Trial Court;
b) The petitioner shall follow the itinerary/schedule annexed with the present application and shall not visit any destination other than those specified in the said itinerary from 20.01.2023 to 08.02.2023;
O.P. Katyal vs State & Anr on 20 January, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/11774291/
2 c) The petitioner shall not exit immigration at the transit points;
d) The petitioner shall furnish his mobile number and email id, at the time of furnishing Bank Guarantee, which shall be kept operational at all times during the period of visit to London (United Kingdom), Dubai (UAE) and Cebu (Philippines);
e) The applicant shall file copy of e-tickets and copy of passport containing the entry regarding his visit upon return.
9.

